#. type: Title #
#: docs/sap/overview.md:1 docs/sap/overview.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "SAP Overview"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/overview.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "**SAP** (Satellite Application Protocol, version `SAP/1.0`) is the WebSocket JSON protocol between the FreeAnima **Hub** (`anima service`) and **Satellite** processes. Satellites are standalone apps (e.g. Chat) that expose their own HTTP UI while delegating agent runtime to the Hub.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/overview.md:10
msgid ""
"Schemas and client SDK live in [`packages/sap-contract/`](../../packages/sap-"
"contract/). Hub server implementation: [`platform/src/sap/`](../../platform/"
"src/sap/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/overview.md:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Design goals"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/overview.md:16
msgid ""
"**One Hub WS per instance**: each satellite instance opens exactly one `/sap/"
"v1` connection to the Hub (multiplex conversations, streams, tools)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/overview.md:16
msgid ""
"**Origin isolation**: bundled clients may use browser-direct Hub WS (`sap-"
"direct`) or a local SAP relay (`/sap/relay/v1`) depending on deployment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/sap/overview.md:16
msgid ""
"**Shared contract**: both sides import `@freeanima/sap-contract` for "
"envelopes, RPC types, `runSapTransport`, `createSapBrowserClient`, and "
"`createSapRelayBrowserClient`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/overview.md:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "Topology"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (mermaid)
#: docs/sap/overview.md:19
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"flowchart LR\n"
"  subgraph chat [Chat satellite]\n"
"    B1[Browser] -->|SAP WS or relay| Hub\n"
"  end\n"
"  Hub --> Runtime[AgentRuntime]\n"
"  subgraph hubAdmin [Hub Admin]\n"
"    Admin[Admin console]\n"
"  end\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/overview.md:35
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Role  | Default                 | Responsibility                                   |\n"
"| ----- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| Hub   | `http://127.0.0.1:2658` | Agent runtime, SAP WebSocket server at `/sap/v1` |\n"
"| Chat  | bundled `/chat`         | Chat UI; SAP direct or relay                     |\n"
"| Admin | bundled shell `/admin`  | Memory, config, tools, satellite status (Hub REST `/api/*`) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/sap/overview.md:37
msgid ""
"See also: [architecture Client UI section](../concepts/"
"architecture.md#client-uibundled)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/sap/overview.md:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "End-to-end happy path"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (mermaid)
#: docs/sap/overview.md:40
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sequenceDiagram\n"
"  participant Sat as Satellite process\n"
"  participant Hub as Hub\n"
"  participant Agent as AgentRuntime\n"
"\n"
"  Sat->>Hub: connect\n"
"  Hub->>Sat: connected\n"
"  Sat->>Hub: req tool.register\n"
"  Hub->>Sat: res ok\n"
"  Sat->>Hub: req conversation.create\n"
"  Hub->>Sat: res conversation_id\n"
"  Sat->>Hub: req message.send\n"
"  Hub->>Sat: res stream_id\n"
"  Hub-->>Sat: evt stream.accepted\n"
"  Hub-->>Sat: evt stream.token\n"
"  Agent->>Hub: invoke sap tool\n"
"  Hub-->>Sat: evt tool.call\n"
"  Sat->>Hub: req tool.result\n"
"  Hub-->>Sat: evt stream.tool_result\n"
"  Hub-->>Sat: evt stream.done\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/sap/overview.md:68
msgid "Satellite process opens `ws://{hub}/sap/v1` and sends `connect`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/sap/overview.md:68
msgid ""
"Hub replies `connected` and registers the instance in `SatelliteManager`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/sap/overview.md:68
msgid "Satellite registers local tools via `tool.register` (if any)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/sap/overview.md:68
msgid "`message.send` returns a `stream_id`; Hub pushes `stream.*` events."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: docs/sap/overview.md:68
msgid ""
"When the agent calls a Satellite tool, Hub sends `tool.call`; Satellite "
"replies with `tool.result` or `tool.error`."
msgstr ""

